          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">LastiSeal</strong> solves the failure mode that ruins most masonry sealers: it puts the protection inside the material, where nothing can peel it off. On porous brick, block or weathered concrete that has been stripped and properly cleaned, that mechanism delivers, and the 15-year warranty is a reasonable reflection of it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            But every one of its advantages depends on penetration, which makes preparation non-negotiable rather than merely advisable. Run the thirty-second water test before you buy anything. If water soaks in, this is a strong choice. If it beads, deal with what is blocking the surface first — because until you do, no penetrating sealer on the market is going to help.
          </p>
